<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58296" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοέω</span></b> , 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοῶ</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mark, perceive, hear</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστρωτος εὕδω καὶ τὰ μὲν πρᾶτ᾽ οὐ
					κοῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					35
				</span></i>
			 (prob.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δ᾽ οὐ κοεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					4.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hellad.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
				<u>Bibl.</u>
				p.531
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκόησεν τοὔνεκεν</span> . .
				<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				53
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				198
			</span></i>: etym. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κοῖος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				17
			</span></i>:—also (from <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοάω</span></b> ) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοᾷ: ἀκούει,
			πεύθεται</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκοᾶμες:
				ἠκούσαμεν, ἐπυθόμεθα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκομεν</span> (sic) . . <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾐσθόμεθα</span>, Id. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοϝ</span>-, cf. Skt. <i>kavis</i> 'wise', Lat.
		<i>caveo.</i>)</div>
